RATIONALE: The evaluation explicitly flags the absence of an on-node chat baseline (baseline a) and relies on published chat numbers while measuring agent traces with a char/4 proxy. This is a severe instrumentation mismatch. Furthermore, the char/4 proxy might artificially inflate the token mass of tool results (which often consist of dense, high-entropy text or code) relative to standard conversational text. An apples-to-apples comparison using the same methodology (either on-node chat with char/4, or true tokenizer for both) is strictly required to validate the structural contrast.
